# Research gate

External research is for facts the repository cannot answer.

## Do not research

- How this repo already implements the pattern. Read the repository.
- Naming, style, or taste the codebase already settles.
- A second opinion on a decision the user already made.

## Do research

- The current contract of a library, API, or product the repo does not
  document
- A deprecation, security advisory, or version constraint that would change
  the plan
- Prior art only when the team has no local pattern and the choice is not
  obvious

## Evidence

- Prefer the vendor's current docs, release notes, or source over a blog or
  an old forum post.
- A forum post is a lead. Confirm it against a primary source before the
  plan depends on it.
- Separate known, disputed, and unknown. Do not smooth a dispute into a
  single confident sentence.
- Cite the source with a title and URL. Do not paste secrets, tokens, or
  private payloads.

## Stop

Stop when the planner can choose a reversible default. Do not keep searching
for a perfect option after a safe default exists.

## Done

The return has an answer; known / disputed / unknown; sources; caveats; and
one implication for the plan.
